===Etymology===
{{prefix|anti|particle|lang=en}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|anti-particle}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈæntiˌpɑɹtɪkəl/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|particle}} A [[subatomic particle]] corresponding to another [[particle]] with the same [[mass]], [[spin]] and [[mean]] [[lifetime]] but with [[charge]], [[parity]], [[strangeness]] and other [[quantum number]]s flipped in sign. This particle is [[antimatter]].
# {{lb|en|physics}} Under Wheeler physics, a time-reversed particle.

